{
  "format": "memory-settings-policy/1",
  "$comment": [
    "The class of every setting and the rules of the second signature. The hash of this file is in the inner anchors (anchors-inner.schema.json, settings_policy_sha256): the policy cannot be replaced from the panel.",
    "class: operational — one administrator, at once; policy — tightening at once, weakening by weaken needs a second signature; anchored — while anchors are in force only through the anchors, without anchors as policy with its own weaken (any — every change) and an alert; immutable — not changed through the API.",
    "weaken: bool_true_to_false | bool_false_to_true | num_increase | num_decrease | enum_order:[a,b,…] (a move towards the start weakens) | list_add | list_remove | any | null.",
    "audit: value — the old and the new value; fingerprint — an HMAC of the value (secrets, customer lists under NDA, certificates); keys_only — only the fact of the change.",
    "where (required for edge.* and admin.*): inside — inside only; edge — goes to the edge through edge_meta.settings; both — both places. On the edge the name has no category prefix; the set is checked against edge-meta.schema.json.",
    "default_off: a dark-launch flag — off on a clean seed: false, \"off\", [], \"\" or off_value. always: in the mode advanced a second signature whatever admin.second_signature says; in basic (security.mode) there are no second signatures — the change applies at once, with the event would_require_approval and an alert.",
    "x-stage: the stage that adds the key to 04-seed.sql (in the same commit, its label in setting-labels.ts and its bound in edge-settings.ts); without x-stage the key is already in the seed. A stage changes only the keys of its own x-stage and appends its own.",
    "Keys are grouped by stage in stage order (keys without x-stage first), with an empty line between groups, so that edits of neighbouring stages merge without conflicts. A stage without keys yet puts its group in its place in that order, also after an empty line."
  ],
